## 2. Product Architecture

Genie consists of three connected layers.

### Frontend

Built using Next.js and TypeScript.

Responsible for:

- Family onboarding and person creation.
- Taste Portrait and Taste Map presentation.
- Wish generation and exploration.
- Wish Circle participation.
- Wish Maker discovery and request tracking.
- Wish Book compilation and sharing.
- Hospice organisation applications and coordination.
- Privacy, consent and retention interfaces.
- Fictional demonstration experiences.

### Backend

Built using FastAPI and Supabase PostgreSQL.

The backend documentation describes persistent support for people, portraits, wishes, Wish Circle contributions, Wish Makers, requests, Wish Books, consent and retention.

It also includes application/review workflows for Wish Makers, private management links, request statuses, contact privacy and organisation coordination.

### Qloo and Agentic Engine

The engine uses Qloo-powered taste resolution to support personalisation and recommendation generation.

Its documented capabilities include:

- Taste resolution and fallback handling.
- Taste Portrait generation.
- Traceable wish recommendations.
- Reaction Mode.
- Comparison experiences.
- Bedside Kit.
- Source and provenance labels.

Genie distinguishes between information directly supplied by a family, reactions, inferred preferences and AI-generated suggestions.

Raw Qloo response data must not be exposed in public documentation or fixtures.

