## 3. Core Product Features

### 3.1 Start a Story

Families can begin a real Genie journey by creating a profile for their loved one.

The onboarding process collects essential details and starts building a personalised experience.

**Route:** `/start`

### 3.2 Taste Portrait and Taste Map

Genie develops an understanding of a person's preferences using information contributed by their family and the Qloo-powered engine.

The interface preserves provenance instead of presenting every recommendation as a confirmed fact.

**Route:** `/person/[id]/taste-map`

### 3.3 Wish Circle

Families can invite relatives and friends to contribute memories, preferences and meaningful information through a private link.

Consent and privacy remain important parts of this process.

### 3.4 Personalised Wishes

Genie uses the available information to suggest experiences that reflect the person's tastes, memories and interests.

Recommendations include supporting information rather than presenting unexplained AI outputs.

**Route:** `/person/[id]/wishes`

### 3.5 Wish Makers

Wish Makers can apply to participate in fulfilling wishes.

The documented workflow includes application review, request management, acceptance/decline and contact privacy.

Real Wish Makers and sample makers must remain clearly distinguishable.

**Routes:**

- `/makers/apply`
- `/maker/recover`
- `/maker/[token]`

### 3.6 Wish Book

The Wish Book brings meaningful information together into a keepsake that families can compile, print and share.

**Routes:**

- `/person/[id]/wish-book`
- `/book/[token]`

### 3.7 Hospice Organisation Portal

Genie also provides an organisation-facing pathway for hospice teams.

It includes a public application page and a private coordination interface covering cases, team members and activity.

**Routes:**

- `/for-hospices`
- `/org/[token]`
- `/org/[token]/cases/[caseKey]`
- `/org/[token]/team`
- `/org/[token]/activity`

